\n    }\n\n    public double getLon() {\n        return lon;\n    }\n\n    public void setLon(double lon) {\n        this.lon = lon;\n    }\n\n    @Override\n    public String toString() {\n        return \"Block - \" + block + \", Time - \" + time + \", Servo1 - \" + degree1 + \", Servo2 - \" + degree2 + \", Servo3 - \" + degree3 + \", Servo4 - \" + degree4 + \", Lat - \" + lat + \", Lon - \" + lon;\n    }\n}\n"}]}}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"0b1a0e2c-6153-48f1-b2b4-fd03aeee58a1","session_id":"ec90641b-cadf-4314-bc40-d7171b153ff0","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"0b1a0e2c-6153-48f1-b2b4-fd03aeee58a1","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can see the bug. Let me analyze the `processDegreeInput` method:\n\n```java\nprivate void processDegreeInput(EditText degreeText, SeekArc seekArc) {\n    int previousDegree = degree;\n    String degreeStr = degreeText.getText().toString().trim();\n\n    if (degreeStr.isEmpty()) {\n        degree = (degree == 0) ? (int) (seekArc.getProgress() * 3.6) : previousDegree;\n    } else {\n        try {\n            degree = Integer.parseInt(degreeStr);\n        } catch (NumberFormatException e) {\n            degreeText.setText(getResources().getString(R.string.zero));\n            seekArc.setProgress(0);\n            toastInvalidValueMessage();\n            return;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (degree > 360 || degree < 0) {\n        degreeText.setText(getResources().getString(R.string.zero));\n        seekArc.setProgress(0);\n        toastInvalidValueMessage();\n    } else {\n        seekArc.setProgress((int) (degree / 3.6));\n        editEnter = true;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe issue is that after parsing the user input and updating the seek bar position, the text field never gets refreshed with the actual degree value. The `editEnter` flag is set to true, but there's no code path that updates the EditText display to reflect what was just set. Looking at the `onProgressChanged` listener, I can see it updates the text field when `editEnter` is true, but that logic needs to be triggered after the seek bar progress is set. The problem is that `seekArc.setProgress()` might not trigger the listener callback if the value doesn't change, so the text never gets updated. Let me trace through the flow: when the user sets Servo 1 to 100 by dragging, `seekArc1` progress becomes 36,